\meta{commit}{cd580b7}
\import{base-macros}

\p{The audit of the reference engine found that the loader drops metadata records, which are part of the official term identity. Under the practical policy that stays as it is: a metadata node is transparent. With the new option \code{\verb~|strictMetadata~}, off by default and meant for the strict policy, every axiom, definition, theorem and opaque constant whose type or value carries metadata is declined per unit; metadata inside inductive and quotient records is declined in both modes, as before. The eight corpora contain no metadata record. With the option off the store digest is identical with that of the loader published before in all 14 reader configurations, and the gate passes with 230 of 230 tests and the published mutant record.}

\p{Detail: \src{rlvm-load/README.md}, \src{docs/design/OWNER-NOTES.md}. Commit \commit{cd580b7}. Session: [exactness](ses-874D). Related: [metadata is declined only in the strict mode](dec-USLM), [metadata in the official term identity](ins-61D4).}
